.TH GHELPER-LINUX 1 "" "g-helper-linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghelper-linux \- performance, fan, GPU and battery control for ASUS laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghelper-linux
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B g-helper-linux
is a compact GTK4/libadwaita control centre for ASUS laptops, modelled on
G-Helper for Windows.  It drives
.BR asusd " (asusctl)"
for performance profiles, fan curves, power limits, keyboard lighting and
battery limits, and
.B cardwire
for runtime GPU blocking.
.PP
Without arguments the main window opens next to the KDE panel.  Only one
instance runs at a time: a second launch forwards its window options to the
running instance and exits.
.PP
The same binary also performs one-shot changes and can run the optional
power-source automation loop.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Window
.TP
.B \-\-page \fIPAGE\fR
Open a specific window:
.IR main ,
.IR fans ,
.I settings
or
.IR hotkeys .
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the tray.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print a JSON diagnostics report (services, firmware attributes, sensors,
hotkeys, battery) and exit.  Useful in bug reports.
.TP
.B \-\-learn\-fn
Print ASUS hotkey key codes until interrupted, one line per key press.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose logging.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SS One-shot actions
These change a setting and exit.  They do not need a running window.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIquiet\fR|\fIbalanced\fR|\fIperformance\fR|\fIcustom\fR
Switch the platform profile.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\-mode \fIintegrated\fR|\fIhybrid\fR|\fIsmart\fR|\fImanual\fR
Set the cardwire GPU mode.
.TP
.B \-\-charge\-limit \fIPERCENT\fR
Set the battery charge limit (20\-100).
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-rate \fIHZ\fR|\fImax\fR
Set the panel refresh rate for the current resolution (KDE).
.SS Automation daemon
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run the power-source automation loop in the foreground.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Run a single automation step and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report what the automation would change without applying it.
.TP
.B \-\-init\-config
Write the default automation configuration file.
.PP
GPU mode automation is off by default: cardwire's own
.B battery_auto_switch
already selects integrated mode on battery and the configured mode on AC.
Enable it in
.I automation.json
only when that switch is turned off.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ghelper-linux/ui.json
Window geometry, preferences, hotkey mappings and the dGPU app list.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ghelper-linux/fan-curves.json
Named fan-curve presets created from the Fans + Power window.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ghelper-linux/automation.json
Configuration for the optional automation daemon.
.SH EXAMPLES
Switch to Silent mode from a script or desktop shortcut:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ghelper-linux \-\-profile quiet
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show the backend report while troubleshooting:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ghelper-linux \-\-check | jq .
.EE
.RE
.PP
Find out what the ROG key sends:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ghelper-linux \-\-learn\-fn
.EE
.RE
.SH HOTKEYS
ASUS hotkeys are read passively from
.IR /dev/input/event* ;
the devices are never grabbed, so every key keeps its normal function.
Reading requires the udev rule installed with
.BR "make install" .
Map keys in
.B Settings \(-> Hotkeys
or with
.BR "\-\-page hotkeys" .
.PP
On the Zephyrus G14 (GA402RK) the ROG/Armoury key reports
.BR KEY_PROG1 ;
other models may report
.BR KEY_PROG3 .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asusd (8),
.BR cardwire (1)
.PP
